#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161678 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162112 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "444ad045-3c7b-5668-bc3a-e3cb49a5b6f2" :knowledge-point/title "Working With the Definition of a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "29e739b1-8745-517f-9011-d1761364c4c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-10099" :question/problem "${(3(x^{2} + y^{2}))/(3x^{2} + 1),\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nConsider the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$, for which the conditional probability density function $f_{Y \\,\\mid \\, X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ and the marginal density function $f_X(x)$ are shown above. Find the expression of the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\,\\mid \\, X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) =\\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_X (x)}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y$, and\n- $f_X (x)$ is the marginal density function for $X$.\n\nFrom the equation above, it follows that\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = f_{Y \\,\\mid \\, X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\cdot f_X (x)\n$$\n\nNow, for\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x, y) &= f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x) \\cdot f_{X}(x) \\\\\n&= (3(x^{2} + y^{2}))/(3x^{2} + 1) \\cdot \\frac{3x^{2} + 1}{2} \\\\\n&= (3(x^{2} + y^{2}))/(2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y$, the function $f_{Y \\,\\mid \\, X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ equals $0$. As a result, the product will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the joint probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{3 (x 2 + y 2) 2,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161679 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "3439786b-905b-5642-89d1-61b0345f79e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10100" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n${8x^{2}y,\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le \\sqrt{x} \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind $P \\left(Y < \\dfrac{1}{2} \\,\\bigg \\mid \\, X=1\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\nP(Y \\in A \\, \\mid \\, X = x) = \\int_A f_{Y \\, \\mid \\, X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\, \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $f_{Y \\, \\mid \\, X} (y \\, \\mid \\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function.\n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $X$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{X}(x) &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}8x^{2}ydy \\\\\n&= 8x^{2}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ydy \\\\\n&= 8x^{2}[\\frac{1}{2}y^{2}]_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\\n&= 4x^{2}(\\sqrt{x})^{2} - 0 \\\\\n&= 4x^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for $f_X(x)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{4x^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\, \\mid \\, X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x) =\\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_X (x)}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y$, and\n- $f_X (x)$ is the marginal density function for $X$.\n\nNow, for\n\n$$\n0< x \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{X}(x)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8x^{2}y}{4x^{3}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2y}{x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y$, the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0$. As a result, $f_{Y \\, \\mid \\, X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{2y}{x},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le \\sqrt{x} \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(Y < \\frac{1}{2} \\mid X = 1) &= \\int_{0}^{1/2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x = 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2y}{1}dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1/2}2ydy \\\\\n&= [y^{2}]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb3b4b6a-3a24-5079-bf33-ed1c5576ffa7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "f1c9e136-57b3-59ae-90e0-b28921be44ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-10101" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n${x + y,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function $f_{X \\, \\mid \\, Y} (x \\, \\mid \\, y)$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}(x + y)dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + xy]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} + y - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{2y + 1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{2y + 1}{2},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_{X \\, \\mid \\, Y} (x \\, \\mid \\, y) = \\dfrac{f(x, y)}{f_Y (y)}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y$, and\n- $f_Y(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y$.\n\nNow, for\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid y) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{Y}(y)) \\\\\n&= (x + y)/((\\frac{2y + 1}{2})) \\\\\n&= (2(x + y))/(2y + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y$, the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0$. As a result, $f_{X \\,\\mid \\, Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{2 (x + y) 2 y + 1,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "184d9e09-3335-5617-8989-e5ab08ca04e7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Conditional Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c35ea81-1fba-5743-bc51-d55ebe9293ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411702} {:answer/id #uuid "4668fa6c-efd9-5349-af00-60d3491fb89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} {:answer/id #uuid "4822c638-df09-5a29-b181-ed51e650cdfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411716} {:answer/id #uuid "debe288e-f7cd-5ceb-8f13-e4258cc3d96c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411803} {:answer/id #uuid "e02c333f-cc9c-5916-848d-431524aca433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4668fa6c-efd9-5349-af00-60d3491fb89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411715} :answer-field/id #uuid "a596b6c7-9c32-5ca9-bbc7-7ea06ecbb649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd343afe-c54e-593d-8dc2-ed57fc5e3a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-143625" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(X\\in A\\,|\\,Y=y)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =P(X<\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
